# ReciFinder Implementation Plan

The objective is to create a complete Flutter mobile app named "ReciFinder" that fetches recipe data from TheMealDB API, manages state using Provider, and follows clean architecture practices. 

## Proposed Changes

### Scaffold setup
- Initialize `recifinder` Flutter project in `C:\Users\Lenovo\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\recifinder`.
- Add dependencies (`http`, `provider`, `cached_network_image`) to `pubspec.yaml`.

### Data Layer
- **[NEW] `lib/models/meal.dart`**: Defines `Meal` model to parse JSON from TheMealDB API. Includes properties like `idMeal`, `strMeal`, `strCategory`, `strArea`, `strInstructions`, `strMealThumb`, and lists for ingredients/measures.
- **[NEW] `lib/services/api_service.dart`**: Contains methods to search for meals by name and lookup meals by ID using `http` package.

### State Management
- **[NEW] `lib/providers/recipe_provider.dart`**: Manages search results, loading states, and error messages. Notifies listeners when state changes.

### UI Layer
- **[NEW] `lib/widgets/recipe_card.dart`**: Reusable card widget displaying recipe image (via `cached_network_image`), name, and category.
- **[NEW] `lib/screens/home_screen.dart`**: Features a search bar, pull-to-refresh (`RefreshIndicator`), and a scrollable list of `RecipeCard`s showing search results. Contains error/loading UI.
- **[NEW] `lib/screens/recipe_detail_screen.dart`**: Displays detailed information about a selected recipe, including a large image, category, area, ingredients list, and cooking instructions.
- **[MODIFY] `lib/main.dart`**: Sets up the app theme, `MultiProvider` for state management, and the root navigation starting at `HomeScreen`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated/Build Verification
- Run `flutter pub get` to resolve dependencies.
- Compile the app using `flutter build apk --release` or `flutter analyze` to ensure no compile-time errors exist.

### Manual Verification
- Provide instructions to the user on how to build and run the application on Android.
